  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">JSB - Building Resilience and Enhancing Food Security of Drought Affected Smallholder Farmers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to enhance food security and build resilience in rural communities by addressing key agricultural challenges. The project will focus on increasing the production of drought-resistant traditional grains such as sorghum, millet, and other resilient crops, which are essential for improving food security in drought-prone areas of Chivi and Mwenezi districts of Zimbabwe. To mitigate the damage caused by crop pests, particularly red-billed quelea birds (Quelea q</narrative>
  </description>
